# jobagent — install with:  crontab /home/dileep/jobagent/crontab-example
# Verify with:              crontab -l
# Remove with:              crontab -r
#
# Cron rather than a systemd --user timer because linger is disabled on this
# box, so user services would stop at logout. A systemd timer is nicer (proper
# logging, restart policy) but needs:  sudo loginctl enable-linger dileep
#
# Absolute paths throughout: cron starts in $HOME with a minimal environment,
# so a bare ./run-daily.sh would not resolve. The script cd's to its own
# directory internally and loads .env itself.
#
# Logs land in ~/jobagent-logs (14-day retention, pruned by the script).
# Failures are also reported to the #job-errors Discord channel.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# Full pass, morning and evening. run-daily.sh takes an flock, so if one run
# overruns into the next the second exits immediately instead of double-claiming.
0 7,19 * * *  /home/dileep/jobagent/run-daily.sh >/dev/null 2>&1

# Midday: discovery and notifications only, no spend. Switch this to a full
# pass once you are happy the A-F scoring behaves.
0 13 * * *    /home/dileep/jobagent/run-daily.sh --no-filter >/dev/null 2>&1
